1. One-time system prerequisites
bash

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y python3-venv python3-pip build-essential
# CUDA dev libs so pycuda can build if needed
sudo apt install -y python3-pycuda

2. Create the RF-DETR venv
bash

python3 -m venv ~/rfdetr-env
source ~/rfdetr-env/bin/activate
pip install --upgrade pip

3. Install dependencies (order matters)
bash

# RF-DETR core + TensorRT/pycuda stack
pip install rfdetr "inference-models[trt10]"

# Then pin torch to CUDA 12.1 to avoid the CUDA 13 segfault
pip uninstall -y torch torchvision
pip install torch==2.5.1 torchvision==0.20.1 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121

4. Verify the stack (all four should pass)
bash

python -c "import torch; print(torch.__version__)"
python -c "import torch; print(torch.version.cuda)"
python -c "import torch; print(torch.cuda.is_available())"
python -c "import torch; print(torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))"
python -c "import tensorrt as trt; print('TRT', trt.__version__); trt.Builder(trt.Logger(trt.Logger.WARNING)); print('Builder OK')"
python -c "import pycuda.autoinit; print('pycuda OK')"

Expect: 2.5.1+cu121, 12.1, True, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU, TRT 10.16.x + Builder OK, pycuda OK.
5. Build the TensorRT engine (one-time, per GPU)
bash

cd ~
python - <<'EOF'
from rfdetr import RFDETRLarge
m = RFDETRLarge()
print("Engine:", m.export(format="trt", output_dir="rfdetr_trt_model"))
EOF

Output should end with something like:
Engine: rfdetr_trt_model/rfdetr-large_fp16.trt

Engine is GPU-specific — rebuild if you change GPU or major TensorRT version.
6. Dry run (preview routing, no files copied)
bash

source ~/rfdetr-env/bin/activate
cd ~
python processor_rfdeter.py \
    -i ~/calibration_images/data \
    -o ~/sorted_test \
    --dry-run

You'll see one line per image (file.jpg -> person/file.jpg) and a final count. Nothing is written to disk.
7. Actual run (copies files into class folders)
bash

python processor_rfdeter.py \
    -i ~/calibration_images/data \
    -o ~/sorted_test

Result:

    ~/sorted_test/person/, ~/sorted_test/car/, etc.

    ~/sorted_test/empty_or_unknown/ for images with no detections

    Original files untouched (copies, not moves)

8. Useful variants

Different confidence threshold (default 0.40):
bash

python processor_rfdeter.py -i ~/Pictures -o ~/Pictures_Sorted --conf 0.25

Run on a large library unattended (survives SSH drop):
bash

tmux new -s sort
# inside tmux:
source ~/rfdetr-env/bin/activate
python processor_rfdeter.py -i ~/Pictures -o ~/Pictures_Sorted
# detach with Ctrl+B then D; reattach with: tmux attach -t sort

Check what landed where afterwards:
bash

find ~/sorted_test -type d
find ~/sorted_test -type f | wc -l

Cheat sheet: activate and run next time
bash

source ~/rfdetr-env/bin/activate
python ~/processor_rfdeter.py -i <source> -o <dest> [--conf 0.4] [--dry-run]

That's the whole loop. The only step you never repeat is Step 5 (engine build) unless you change GPU/TensorRT. 🙂
